  "query_preview": "..\n\nNext 7 Days (Through Sunday)...\n\nMainly dry conditions will prevail over the area today as\nshortwave ridging builds into the region. A few sprinkles or\nisolated showers are possible over the far southeast in the\nafternoon, though the chance is low (less than 15%). As a trough\npushes inland into the the Pac NW, a low level jet looks to set up\nover the east tonight, with the potential for a few showers and\nperhaps a thunderstorm, though the best chances are into northeast\nMT. \n\nAs the upper trough pushes into the northern Rockies Tuesday, \nunsettled conditions are expected to develop, continuing through \nmuch of the week ahead. Occasional shortwaves dropping through the\nregion will bring daily chances for showers and thunderstorms,\ngreatest on Tuesday/Tuesday night (40-90% chance). Breezy west to\nnorthwest winds could move across the area at times as well. \nTemperatures may be cool enough for some light snow in the high \ncountry, especially Tuesday night into Wednesday and the upcoming \nweekend. This includes the Beartooth Hwy. Those with recreation \nplans in the mountains should pay attention to the forecast. The \nchance for strong to severe storms looks to remain low through the\nweek, with the better chance east of the area. Temperatures are \nforecast to range from the 70s to near 80 degrees today and the \nlower 70s to lower 80s Tuesday. Temperatures then drop into the \n60s to middle 70s for the remainder of the week. STP",
